---
const pageTitle = "Sponsors — Barkly Labs";
const pageDescription =
  "Support Barkly Labs and help build human-centered technology, research infrastructure, hardware, software, and open systems.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <title>{pageTitle}</title>

    <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#050505" />

    <meta property="og:title" content={pageTitle} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={pageDescription} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.barklylabs.space/sponsors" />

    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.barklylabs.space/sponsors" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a href="/" class="header-logo" aria-label="Barkly Labs home">
        <span>BARKLY</span>
        <span>LABS</span>
      </a>

      <nav class="header-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/">HOME</a>
        <a href="/about">ABOUT</a>
        <a href="/support">SUPPORT</a>
        <a href="/sponsors">SPONSORS</a>
      </nav>

      <div class="header-status">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        <span>LAB STATUS / ACTIVE</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav class="side-nav" aria-label="Page sections">
      <a href="#why">
        <span>01</span>
        WHY
      </a>

      <a href="#enable">
        <span>02</span>
        ENABLE
      </a>

      <a href="#models">
        <span>03</span>
        MODELS
      </a>

      <a href="#standard">
        <span>04</span>
        STANDARD
      </a>

      <a href="#resources">
        <span>05</span>
        RESOURCES
      </a>

      <a href="#contact">
        <span>06</span>
        CONTACT
      </a>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <!-- =========================================================
           HERO
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="hero">
        <div class="section-meta">
          <span>SPONSORSHIP</span>
          <span>/</span>
          <span>BARKLY LABS</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-title">
          <div class="eyebrow">
            <span>01 / INFRASTRUCTURE FOR WHAT COMES NEXT</span>
          </div>

          <h1>
            SPONSOR<br />
            <span>THE LAB.</span>
          </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <p class="hero-copy">
            Barkly Labs builds human-centered technology, research
            infrastructure, hardware, software, documentation, and
            experimental systems designed around the people who use them.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-mark">
            PEOPLE ARE WORTH<br />
            DESIGNING FOR.<br />
            <br />
            TECHNOLOGY SHOULD<br />
            ADAPT TO HUMANS.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           WHY SPONSOR
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="content-section" id="why">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="section-number">01</div>

          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
              WHY SPONSOR BARKLY
            </div>

            <h2>
              SPONSORSHIP IS
              <span>INFRASTRUCTURE.</span>
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-body">
          <p class="large-copy">
            Sponsorship is not just a contribution to a project.
            It is infrastructure for experimentation.
          </p>

          <p>
            Barkly Labs exists to explore what happens when technology is
            designed around human needs instead of forcing humans to adapt
            themselves to complicated systems.
          </p>

          <p>
            A sponsorship can become compute, hardware, software,
            accessibility work, research, documentation, testing,
            infrastructure, or time.
          </p>

          <p>
            Those resources allow ideas to move from prototype to working
            system — and from working system to something other people can
            understand, use, study, modify, and build upon.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           WHAT SPONSORS ENABLE
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="content-section" id="enable">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="section-number">02</div>

          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
              RESOURCE PIPELINE
            </div>

            <h2>
              WHAT SPONSORS
              <span>ENABLE.</span>
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-body">
          <p class="large-copy">
            Resources become systems.
            Systems become tools.
            Tools become possibilities.
          </p>

          <p>
            Sponsorship helps Barkly build the underlying infrastructure
            required to experiment seriously: computers, servers, hardware,
            development environments, research systems, documentation,
            accessibility tooling, and public-facing projects.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="system-grid">
          <article class="system-card">
            <div class="system-top">
              <span>01</span>
              <span>COMPUTE</span>
            </div>

            <h3>COMPUTE</h3>

            <p>
              Local AI, model experimentation, build infrastructure,
              testing, development environments, and the computing
              resources required to turn ideas into working systems.
            </p>

            <div class="tag-list">
              <span>AI</span>
              <span>LOCAL COMPUTE</span>
              <span>TESTING</span>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="system-card">
            <div class="system-top">
              <span>02</span>
              <span>HARDWARE</span>
            </div>

            <h3>HARDWARE</h3>

            <p>
              Prototypes, embedded systems, experimental computers,
              sensors, interfaces, robotics, recycled hardware, and
              infrastructure for physical experimentation.
            </p>

            <div class="tag-list">
              <span>PROTOTYPING</span>
              <span>EMBEDDED</span>
              <span>OPEN HARDWARE</span>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="system-card">
            <div class="system-top">
              <span>03</span>
              <span>RESEARCH</span>
            </div>

            <h3>RESEARCH</h3>

            <p>
              Human-centered engineering research, experiments,
              benchmarks, standards development, technical investigation,
              and evidence-driven exploration.
            </p>

            <div class="tag-list">
              <span>RESEARCH</span>
              <span>EXPERIMENTAL</span>
              <span>EVIDENCE</span>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="system-card">
            <div class="system-top">
              <span>04</span>
              <span>SOFTWARE</span>
            </div>

            <h3>SOFTWARE</h3>

            <p>
              Open systems, developer tooling, APIs, automation,
              documentation systems, infrastructure, and software that
              makes complex technology easier to work with.
            </p>

            <div class="tag-list">
              <span>OPEN SOURCE</span>
              <span>TOOLS</span>
              <span>AUTOMATION</span>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="system-card">
            <div class="system-top">
              <span>05</span>
              <span>ACCESSIBILITY</span>
            </div>

            <h3>ACCESS</h3>

            <p>
              Technology designed around cognitive load, accessibility,
              understandable interfaces, human limitations, and the
              reality that people have different needs.
            </p>

            <div class="tag-list">
              <span>ACCESSIBILITY</span>
              <span>COGNITIVE LOAD</span>
              <span>HUMAN FIRST</span>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="system-card">
            <div class="system-top">
              <span>06</span>
              <span>DOCUMENTATION</span>
            </div>

            <h3>DOCUMENTATION</h3>

            <p>
              Public technical documentation that makes systems easier
              to understand, inspect, reproduce, maintain, and build
              upon.
            </p>

            <div class="tag-list">
              <span>DOCS</span>
              <span>TRANSPARENCY</span>
              <span>KNOWLEDGE</span>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           SPONSORSHIP MODELS
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="content-section" id="models">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="section-number">03</div>

          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
              SPONSORSHIP MODELS
            </div>

            <h2>
              MANY WAYS TO
              <span>BUILD.</span>
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="section-lead">
          Barkly sponsorship does not need to fit into a single box.
          Different resources can support different parts of the
          laboratory. The goal is simple: put useful resources where
          they can create useful systems.
        </p>

        <div class="pipeline">
          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">01</div>

            <div>
              <h3>INFRASTRUCTURE SPONSOR</h3>

              <p>
                Help provide servers, compute, hosting, networking,
                storage, development infrastructure, or other foundational
                resources.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">02</div>

            <div>
              <h3>PROJECT SPONSOR</h3>

              <p>
                Support a specific Barkly project and help move it from
                experimentation toward a usable public system.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">03</div>

            <div>
              <h3>HARDWARE SPONSOR</h3>

              <p>
                Provide computers, components, development boards,
                sensors, networking equipment, tools, or other physical
                resources.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">04</div>

            <div>
              <h3>RESEARCH SPONSOR</h3>

              <p>
                Help fund experiments, engineering research, standards,
                benchmarks, documentation, and new technical directions.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">05</div>

            <div>
              <h3>ACCESS SPONSOR</h3>

              <p>
                Support accessibility, community infrastructure,
                educational resources, and technology designed for
                people who are often overlooked.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           SPONSORSHIP OPERATIONS
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="content-section" id="operations">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="section-number">04</div>

          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
              HOW RESOURCES MOVE
            </div>

            <h2>
              BUILD THE
              <span>SYSTEM.</span>
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="operations-layout">
          <div class="operations-copy">
            <p class="large-copy">
              Sponsorship should produce something people can actually
              see, understand, and use.
            </p>

            <p>
              Barkly treats resources as part of an engineering system.
              Contributions should be connected to real infrastructure,
              research, development, accessibility, operations, or
              community work.
            </p>

            <p>
              As Barkly's financial and operational systems mature,
              sponsorship information can be connected to the same
              documentation and reporting infrastructure used throughout
              the laboratory.
            </p>

            <p>
              The goal is not to create a black box around funding.
              The goal is to make the system understandable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="system-launch">
            <div class="launch-header">
              <div>
                <span class="panel-label">RESOURCE FLOW</span>
                <strong>BARKLY SPONSORSHIP SYSTEM</strong>
              </div>

              <span class="status-live">ACTIVE</span>
            </div>

            <div class="launch-body">
              <span class="launch-number">
                SYSTEM / 04
              </span>

              <h3>
                RESOURCE
                <span>→</span>
                SYSTEM
              </h3>

              <p>
                Sponsorship becomes infrastructure, research, development,
                documentation, accessibility, and public technology.
              </p>

              <a class="launch-button" href="/support">
                <span>VIEW SUPPORT SYSTEM</span>
                <span>→</span>
              </a>
            </div>

            <div class="launch-footer">
              <span>TRANSPARENCY / REQUIRED</span>
              <span>HUMAN OVERSIGHT / REQUIRED</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           BARKLY STANDARD
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="content-section" id="standard">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="section-number">05</div>

          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
              BARKLY STANDARD
            </div>

            <h2>
              THE STANDARD
              <span>DOES NOT CHANGE.</span>
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-body">
          <p class="large-copy">
            Sponsorship does not buy control over the people using
            the technology.
          </p>

          <p>
            Barkly Labs is built around the principle that people are
            worth designing for. Financial support should strengthen
            that mission — not weaken it.
          </p>

          <p>
            Sponsors can help provide resources, expertise, infrastructure,
            equipment, and opportunity. The underlying human-centered
            principles remain the same.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="principles-grid">
          <article class="principle-card">
            <span class="card-number">01</span>

            <h3>HUMAN FIRST</h3>

            <p>
              Technology should serve people. People should not have to
              reorganize their lives around technology.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="principle-card">
            <span class="card-number">02</span>

            <h3>UNDERSTANDABLE</h3>

            <p>
              Systems should be explainable. Documentation should expose
              how things work instead of hiding complexity behind a wall.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="principle-card">
            <span class="card-number">03</span>

            <h3>PRIVATE WHERE PRACTICAL</h3>

            <p>
              Personal information and sensitive systems should be treated
              with care, restraint, and respect for the people involved.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="principle-card">
            <span class="card-number">04</span>

            <h3>EXPERIMENTAL</h3>

            <p>
              Barkly is a laboratory. New ideas are allowed to be tested,
              measured, documented, changed, and sometimes abandoned.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="principle-card">
            <span class="card-number">05</span>

            <h3>TRANSPARENT</h3>

            <p>
              Resources, systems, limitations, experiments, and outcomes
              should become easier to understand as the laboratory grows.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="principle-card">
            <span class="card-number">06</span>

            <h3>NON-MANIPULATIVE</h3>

            <p>
              Technology should not rely on confusing people, exploiting
              cognitive limitations, or taking control away from them.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           RESOURCE PIPELINE
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="content-section" id="resources">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div class="section-number">06</div>

          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">
              THE RESOURCE PIPELINE
            </div>

            <h2>
              SHOW THE
              <span>NUMBERS.</span>
            </h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="section-lead">
          Barkly is building toward a financial system where resources
          can be preserved, normalized, reconciled, documented, and
          summarized without turning financial reporting into a black box.
        </p>

        <div class="pipeline">
          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">01</div>

            <div>
              <h3>SPONSORSHIP</h3>

              <p>
                Resources enter the laboratory through sponsorship,
                donations, grants, partnerships, or other legitimate
                sources of support.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">02</div>

            <div>
              <h3>RECORD</h3>

              <p>
                Original financial and operational records remain the
                source material for the system.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">03</div>

            <div>
              <h3>NORMALIZE</h3>

              <p>
                Transactions can be converted into structured information
                while preserving their original source.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">04</div>

            <div>
              <h3>RECONCILE</h3>

              <p>
                Financial records should be checked against their source
                rather than relying on generated summaries alone.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">05</div>

            <div>
              <h3>EXPLAIN</h3>

              <p>
                Automated systems may help explain financial information,
                but the underlying calculations remain deterministic and
                traceable.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-number">06</div>

            <div>
              <h3>PUBLISH</h3>

              <p>
                Where appropriate, useful financial summaries can become
                part of Barkly's public documentation and accountability
                infrastructure.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =========================================================
           CONTACT / FINAL
           ========================================================= -->

      <section class="final-section" id="contact">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>SPONSORSHIP / CONTACT</span>
          <span>/</span>
          <span>BARKLY LABS</span>
        </div>

        <h2>
          HELP BUILD
          <span>THE LAB.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          FUND INFRASTRUCTURE. SUPPORT EXPERIMENTATION. DESIGN FOR PEOPLE.
        </p>

        <a class="final-system-button" href="/contact">
          <span>START WITH BARKLY SUPPORT</span>
          <span>→</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  :global(:root) {
    --sponsor-bg: #050505;
    --sponsor-panel: #0a0a0a;
    --sponsor-panel-raised: #0f0f0f;
    --sponsor-panel-hover: #131313;

    --sponsor-text: #f1f1f1;
    --sponsor-white: #f1f1f1;
    --sponsor-muted: #a1a1a1;
    --sponsor-dim: #686868;
    --sponsor-faint: #444;

    --sponsor-line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    --sponsor-line-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);

    /* BARKLY SPONSOR PINK */
    --sponsor-pink: #ff2f92;
    --sponsor-pink-soft: rgba(255, 47, 146, 0.1);
    --sponsor-pink-line: rgba(255, 47, 146, 0.42);

    --sponsor-max: 1500px;
  }

  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  :global(html) {
    scroll-behavior: smooth !important;
    background: #050505 !important;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0 !important;
    background: #050505 !important;
    color: #f1f1f1 !important;

    font-family:
      Inter,
      system-ui,
      -apple-system,
      BlinkMacSystemFont,
      "Segoe UI",
      sans-serif !important;
  }

  :global(a) {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     SPONSORS PAGE ROOT
     ========================================================= */

  .sponsors-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: #050505 !important;
    color: #f1f1f1 !important;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     HEADER
     ========================================================= */

  .site-header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 100;

    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: center;

    min-height: 70px;
    padding: 0 40px;

    background: rgba(5, 5, 5, 0.96) !important;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12) !important;

    backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  }

  .header-logo {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.18em;
    width: fit-content;

    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .header-logo span:first-child {
    color: #ff2f92 !important;
  }

  .header-logo span:last-child {
    color: #f1f1f1 !important;
  }

  .header-nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 28px;

    font-family:
      "IBM Plex Mono",
      "SFMono-Regular",
      Consolas,
      monospace;

    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .header-nav a {
    color: #a1a1a1 !important;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }

  .header-nav a:hover {
    color: #ff2f92 !important;
  }

  .header-status {
    justify-self: end;

    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;

    font-family:
      "IBM Plex Mono",
      monospace;

    font-size: 9px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;

    color: #a1a1a1 !important;
  }

  .status-dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;

    background: #ff2f92 !important;

    box-shadow:
      0 0 12px rgba(255, 47, 146, 0.65) !important;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     SIDE NAV
     ========================================================= */

  .side-nav {
    position: fixed;
    left: 28px;
    top: 50%;

    transform: translateY(-50%);
    z-index: 20;

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .side-nav a {
    display: flex;
    gap: 9px;

    font-family:
      "IBM Plex Mono",
      monospace;

    font-size: 9px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;

    color: #686868 !important;
  }

  .side-nav a:hover {
    color: #ff2f92 !important;
  }

  .side-nav span {
    color: #ff2f92 !important;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     MAIN
     ========================================================= */

  main {
    width: min(100%, 1500px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #050505 !important;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     HERO
     ========================================================= */

  .hero {
    min-height: 88vh;

    padding: 80px 8vw 90px;

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;

    background: #050505 !important;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12) !important;
  }

  .section-meta,
  .eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    gap: 18px;

    font-family:
      "IBM Plex Mono",
      "SFMono-Regular",
      Consolas,
      monospace;

    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;

    color: #a1a1a1 !important;
  }

  .hero-title {
    margin-top: 13vh;
  }

  .hero-title h1 {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 28px 0 0;

    color: #f1f1f1 !important;

    font-size: clamp(70px, 10vw, 155px);
    line-height: 0.86;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
  }

  .hero-title h1 span {
    color: #ff2f92 !important;
  }

  .hero-bottom {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 220px;
    gap: 80px;

    margin-top: 100px;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 680px;

    color: #a1a1a1 !important;

    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 26px);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .hero-mark {
    align-self: end;

    font-family:
      "IBM Plex Mono",
      monospace;

    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;

